  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Apoyo a las poblaciones clave de mayor riesgo al VIH:2016-2018 - Dominican Republic (01-Jan-2016-31-Dec-2018)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Dominican Republic, HIV, Consejo Nacional para el VIH y el SIDA (CONAVIHSIDA)This program has the following goals: To reduce new infections in key populations and to increase life expectancy of PLHIV in the Dominican Republic in a sustainable manner. The objectives of this program are: Contribute to strengthening STI and HIV/AIDS prevention and education programs, with an emphasis on human rights, gender equality and respect for different sexual orientations and gender identities, through community co-management and participation of key populations.  Increase equal access to care, treatment and support services that promote health and ensure the retention of PLHIV throughout the HIV Treatment Cascade and deliver lasting suppression of viral load.</narrative>
  </description>
